The scripts here are run by testdata/sqllogic.paslang, the runner of sqllogictest's format
(sqlite.org/sqllogictest, D. Richard Hipp) over `uses sqlite`.

evidence_*.test are the scripts of sqllogictest's test/evidence directory (public domain: "you can
redistribute it and/or modify the code as you see fit. No attribution is required", its COPYRIGHT.md),
with their carriage returns taken out except evidence_crlf_createview.test, which keeps them.

gen_*.test are made by scripts/gen_sqllogic.py (the seed and the number of queries in the first line):
random tables, data, statements and queries, the answers SQLite's own (the sqlite3 module of Python over
the system's libsqlite3, the version the first line names). `make check` makes them again when that
version is the system's.

list.txt names the scripts the golden test runs, one on each line.
